  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\nThe characters {瓦|かわら} (roof tile) and {解|かい} (to break apart) combine to evoke the image of tiles falling from a collapsing building.\n\nFORMS:\n{瓦解|がかい}する - to collapse, disintegrate\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {瓦解|がかい}する - to collapse\n- {瓦解|がかい}の{危機|きき} - crisis of collapse\n- {瓦解|がかい}に{瀕|ひん}する - to be on the verge of collapse\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {崩壊|ほうかい} - collapse, breakdown (more common)\n- {解体|かいたい} - dismantling, dissolution",
